      "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which website builder is best in 2026?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The best website builder in 2026 depends on your use case. Webflow is best for professional designers who want pixel-perfect control, a real CMS, and clean code export. Framer is best for interactive marketing sites with modern animations and AI-assisted layout. WordPress is best for blogs, SEO-led publishers, and plugin flexibility. Squarespace is best for small businesses and creators that want polished templates without design work. Wix is best for absolute beginners on a budget who want drag-and-drop everything in one bill." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is Webflow or Framer easier to use?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Framer is easier to start with and feels more modern. Its canvas is familiar to Figma users, the AI layout assistant ships usable sections, and animations, scroll-triggered effects, and responsive breakpoints have a gentler learning curve. Webflow has a steeper onboarding because the Designer reflects HTML/CSS mental models (box model, flexbox, grid, classes, combo classes) and the panel-based styling takes weeks to master. Once mastered, Webflow gives cleaner, more predictable production output and a more mature CMS. Designers typically prefer Webflow; marketers and solo founders often prefer Framer." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which website builder has the best SEO?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "WordPress has the highest SEO ceiling because you control every layer with plugins like Yoast SEO, Rank Math, and Redirection, plus page speed tuning through caching and image optimization. Webflow has the strongest native SEO among SaaS builders — clean semantic HTML, XML sitemaps, robots.txt, metadata per collection item, CDN and SSL by default, and no code bloat from page builders. Framer's SEO is solid but more basic; Squarespace SEO is adequate but less granular; Wix has improved SEO dramatically since switching to full SSR but still lags Webflow and WordPress on technical SEO." } },
