      <h2 id="how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</h2>
      <p>We evaluated the five most-reviewed website builders on the market based on vendor documentation, community consensus, pricing pages, feature comparisons, and public migration case studies. Each builder was assessed against the <a href="/how-we-test/">ToolStep review protocol</a> on time to first publish, visual customization without code, CMS and collection modeling, native SEO controls, page speed output (Lighthouse metrics for equivalent starter templates), app/plugin markets, and developer export or API options.</p>

      <h2 id="ranking-methodology">Ranking Methodology</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Design Flexibility (25%)</strong> — Layout control, responsive breakpoints, animation/interaction, and freedom from template constraints</li>
        <li><strong>Ease of Use (20%)</strong> — Onboarding, learning curve, time from signup to a polished published site</li>
        <li><strong>CMS &amp; Collections (15%)</strong> — Collection modeling, content relationships, multi-author, import/export, and blog capability</li>
        <li><strong>SEO &amp; Performance (15%)</strong> — Semantic HTML output, metadata, sitemaps, robots control, redirects, and Lighthouse scores</li>
        <li><strong>Pricing &amp; Value (15%)</strong> — Free plan, entry tier, bandwidth/CMS limits, and cost for a 50-page site with a blog</li>
        <li><strong>Developer &amp; Export (10%)</strong> — Code export, API access, staging/versioning, and team/collaboration features</li>
      </ul>

