      <h2 id="best-pro-webflow">#1 — Webflow (Best for Professional Designers &amp; Agencies)</h2>
      <p>Webflow ranks #1 as the best website builder for professional designers and agencies in 2026 because it combines visual canvas design with real HTML/CSS output, a production-grade CMS with collection relationships, and clean, semantic, accessible markup that loads fast without builder bloat. Webflow's Designer reflects the real box model — flexbox, grid, classes, combo classes, pseudo-states, and responsive breakpoints at four widths. Once you learn the Designer, you can build production sites that do not require a developer to rewrite.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is the learning curve. New users without a CSS mental model find Webflow overwhelming for the first 1–2 weeks. The CMS is powerful but has item and volume caps on lower tiers, and the free tier ships Webflow branding on a webflow.io subdomain. For agencies, freelance designers, and in-house marketing design teams, Webflow is the strongest long-term investment because sites stay maintainable across teams for years.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Webflow</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Pixel-perfect visual HTML/CSS</strong> — No code bloating; semantic output with CSS classes</li>
          <li><strong>Production CMS</strong> — Collections, multi-reference fields, conditional visibility, multi-author</li>
          <li><strong>Clean performance</strong> — Fast CDN, image optimization, and markup you would hand-write</li>
          <li><strong>Staging + Versioning</strong> — Restore snapshots and test changes before publish</li>
          <li><strong>Agency/Team seats</strong> — Mature team plans, workspaces, and client billing</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://webflow.com" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Start with Webflow Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-interactive-framer">#2 — Framer (Best Modern Interactive Builder)</h2>
      <p>Framer is the fastest-growing website builder in 2026 because its canvas feels like Figma for production sites. Animations, scroll effects, hover states, variants, component props, and AI-assisted layout (Framer AI can ship an entire landing page section in one prompt) make Framer the best choice for interactive marketing sites and product launches where visual motion is the brand. Framer also ships a usable CMS with collection fields and a blog, and it publishes to a global CDN with solid Lighthouse scores.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is ecosystem maturity. Framer's CMS has less granular control over relationships and modeling than Webflow, its SEO toolbox is more basic, and the pool of experienced Framer freelancers and agencies is smaller than Webflow. For landing-page-heavy marketing sites, Framer is the strongest choice. For CMS-heavy sites with thousands of pages and complex collection modeling, Webflow is still the safer bet.</p>
      <p>Deep dive: <a href="/reviews/framer-vs-webflow/">Framer vs Webflow full comparison</a> covering animations, CMS, pricing, and designer workflows.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Framer</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Figma-like canvas</strong> — Familiar to modern product designers</li>
          <li><strong>AI-assisted layout</strong> — Describe a section; Framer builds it</li>
          <li><strong>Best interactions</strong> — Variants, scroll triggers, and motion built in</li>
          <li><strong>Components + props</strong> — Reusable design systems across pages</li>
          <li><strong>Publish to CDN</strong> — Fast global hosting, free subdomain, or custom domain</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://www.framer.com" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Start with Framer Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-cms-wordpress">#3 — WordPress (Best for CMS, Blogging &amp; SEO)</h2>
      <p>WordPress is the original website builder and still the category leader by market share (roughly 40% of all websites) because its block editor (Gutenberg), page builders like Elementor Pro and Beaver Builder, plugin ecosystem, and CMS flexibility are unmatched. WordPress shines when your site is content-first — blog, magazine, publisher, portfolio with case studies, SEO landing pages, or membership/LMS properties. You can combine a blog, knowledge base, forums, and commerce in one install.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is design fragmentation and performance drag. Page builders, custom themes, and plugins frequently conflict, and the most popular WordPress sites require managed hosting, caching layers, and image optimization to hit acceptable Core Web Vitals. For pure marketing sites that do not lean on CMS depth, Webflow or Framer deliver a cleaner output with less operations work.</p>
      <p>See: <a href="/reviews/wordpress-vs-webflow/">WordPress vs Webflow full comparison</a> for design, SEO, plugins, and performance trade-offs.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>WordPress</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Deepest CMS</strong> — Posts, pages, custom post types, taxonomies, multilingual</li>
          <li><strong>60,000+ plugins</strong> — SEO, forms, forums, membership, commerce, booking, LMS</li>
          <li><strong>Highest SEO ceiling</strong> — Yoast / Rank Math give control over every tag and schema</li>
          <li><strong>Largest talent pool</strong> — WordPress developers are easy to hire globally</li>
          <li><strong>Page builders</strong> — Elementor, Divi, and Gutenberg blocks cover most visual needs</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://wordpress.org" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Get WordPress Free</a>
