      <h2 id="best-small-business-squarespace">#4 — Squarespace (Best Small-Business Templates)</h2>
      <p>Squarespace is the best website builder for small businesses, photographers, designers, and creators who want the most polished default templates and one bill for hosting, domain, template, and email campaigns. Every Squarespace template looks premium on publish day without custom tweaks. The Fluid Engine design tool gives point-and-click customization with full CSS access on higher tiers, and Squarespace Email Campaigns, scheduling, invoicing, and member areas cover most small-business marketing workflows.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is escape flexibility. Squarespace sites are harder to migrate from — pages, CSS, and layouts are tightly bound to templates. Squarespace SEO improved in 2025/2026 but is still not as granular as Webflow or WordPress. For small catalogs under 200 products and brands where visual presentation is the primary buying factor, Squarespace is the fastest path to a beautiful site.</p>
      <p>Deep dive: <a href="/reviews/squarespace-vs-wix/">Squarespace vs Wix full comparison</a> for templates, ease of use, pricing, and features.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Squarespace</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Best default templates</strong> — Agency-quality designs out of the box</li>
          <li><strong>All-in-one billing</strong> — Hosting, template, domain, email, and scheduling</li>
          <li><strong>Fluid Engine</strong> — Visual CSS grid layout with responsive drag-and-drop</li>
          <li><strong>Unlimited bandwidth</strong> — No surprise overage charges on traffic spikes</li>
          <li><strong>Built-in marketing</strong> — Email campaigns, scheduling, and member areas</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://www.squarespace.com" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Start Squarespace Trial</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-beginner-wix">#5 — Wix (Best Absolute Beginner Value)</h2>
      <p>Wix is the best website builder for absolute beginners and microbusinesses because its free tier is genuinely usable (free subdomain, no trial expiry), the Wix ADI (Artificial Design Intelligence) can build an entire draft site from answers to a handful of questions, and the drag-and-drop Editor supports absolute positioning — if you can imagine a layout, you can drag it into place without learning flexbox. Wix also bundles forms, bookings, ecommerce (Wix Stores), and video via one Wix account.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is code quality and long-term maintainability. Wix historically struggled with output bloat and SEO — the platform has improved substantially since rolling out full server-side rendering in 2024, but the SEO toolbox is still not in Webflow's or WordPress's league, and agencies rarely recommend Wix for sites above 50 pages. For single-founder businesses on a zero-dollar launch budget, Wix is a credible first website.</p>

